  "raw": " about half an hour long, only the second single from l’s 1982 album T ER e G L E S OU L, a record that contained such gems as “Fly Away” (that jingling piano riff is actually worth getting to know) and simply titled “Got to Get You Into My Life.” Freddie was just in his mid-40s by then; he’d recently been knighted of all things , which somehow rubbed him the wrong way. One can certainly imagine what would go through a man at 40 when some nouveau riche royal like a shonen Jump character springs up outta nowhere calling himself king! With most of Prince's crew already having been turned into nerds for their novels, movies and commercials by the time they were 29 years old, his transition threatened to punish kingdom-building as sensation-based celebrity; backyards not enough for these dogs? Well, he finally came, he saw…and he sliced off",
